  <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
  <title>Cat FAQ</title>
  <style>
    :root {
      color-scheme: dark;
      --bg: #0b1020;
      --panel: #121a2d;
      --panel-2: #17213a;
      --border: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.1);
      --text: #e7ecf7;
      --muted: #a8b2c7;
      --accent: #7c9cff;
      --accent-strong: #9cb2ff;
      --shadow: 0 24px 60px rgba(0, 0, 0, 0.35);
    }

    * {
      box-sizing: border-box;
    }

    body {
      margin: 0;
      min-height: 100vh;
      font-family: Inter, system-ui, -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, "Segoe UI", sans-serif;
      background:
        radial-gradient(circle at top, rgba(124, 156, 255, 0.18), transparent 35%),
        linear-gradient(180deg, #0b1020 0%, #090d18 100%);
      color: var(--text);
      display: grid;
      place-items: center;
      padding: 32px 16px;
    }

    .faq {
      width: min(760px, 100%);
      background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(18, 26, 45, 0.96), rgba(13, 19, 33, 0.96));
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 24px;
      box-shadow: var(--shadow);
      padding: 28px;
    }

    .eyebrow {
      margin: 0 0 10px;
      color: var(--accent-strong);
      font-size: 0.875rem;
      letter-spacing: 0.12em;
      text-transform: uppercase;
    }

    h1 {
      margin: 0 0 8px;
      font-size: clamp(2rem, 4vw, 3rem);
      line-height: 1.1;
    }

    .intro {
      margin: 0 0 24px;
      color: var(--muted);
      line-height: 1.6;
      max-width: 60ch;
    }

    .example {
      border: 1px solid var(--border);
      border-radius: 18px;
      background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.02);
      overflow: hidden;
      margin-top: 14px;
    }

    .question {
      width: 100%;
      appearance: none;
      border: 0;
      background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(23, 33, 58, 0.95), rgba(18, 26, 45, 0.95));
      color: var(--text);
      font: inherit;
      font-weight: 650;
      text-align: left;
      padding: 18px 20px;
      display: flex;
      align-items: center;
      justify-content: space-between;
      gap: 16px;
      cursor: pointer;
    }

    .question:focus-visible {
      outline: 3px solid rgba(124, 156, 255, 0.45);
      outline-offset: -3px;
    }

    .question:hover {
      background: linear-gradient(180deg, rgba(28, 40, 69, 0.98), rgba(21, 31, 54, 0.98));
    }

    .question-text {
      font-size: 1.02rem;
    }

    .icon {
      flex: 0 0 auto;
      width: 32px;
      height: 32px;
      border-radius: 999px;
      display: grid;
      place-items: center;
      background: rgba(124, 156, 255, 0.12);
      color: var(--accent-strong);
      transition: transform 180ms ease, background 180ms ease;
    }

    .example.open .icon {
      transform: rotate(45deg);
      background: rgba(124, 156, 255, 0.2);
    }

    .details {
      padding: 0 20px 18px;
      color: var(--muted);
      line-height: 1.7;
    }

    .details[hidden] {
      display: none;
    }

    .details p {
      margin: 0;
    }

    @media (max-width: 640px) {
      .faq {
        padding: 20px;
        border-radius: 20px;
      }

      .question {
        padding: 16px;
      }

      .details {
        padding: 0 16px 16px;
      }
    }
  </style>
</head>
<body>
  <main class="faq" aria-labelledby="faq-title">
    <p class="eyebrow">Cat care</p>
    <h1 id="faq-title">Frequently asked questions about cats</h1>
    <p class="intro">Tap a question to reveal the answer. Each answer starts collapsed so the page stays tidy and easy to scan.</p>

    <div class="example">
      <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-1">
        <span class="question-text">Why do cats purr?</span>
        <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
      </button>
      <div class="details" id="answer-1" hidden>
        <p>Cats purr for comfort, communication, and sometimes to self-soothe. A relaxed cat often purrs when being petted or resting near someone they trust.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="example">
      <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-2">
        <span class="question-text">How much sleep do cats need?</span>
        <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
      </button>
      <div class="details" id="answer-2" hidden>
        <p>Most cats sleep 12 to 16 hours a day, and some kittens or seniors sleep even more. Their energy comes in bursts, so they alternate between naps and short play sessions.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="example">
      <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-3">
        <span class="question-text">Do cats need a lot of attention?</span>
        <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
      </button>
      <div class="details" id="answer-3" hidden>
        <p>Cats are often independent, but they still need daily interaction, play, and affection on their terms. A few focused minutes each day helps them stay social and mentally engaged.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="example">
      <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-4">
        <span class="question-text">Why do cats knead with their paws?</span>
        <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
      </button>
      <div class="details" id="answer-4" hidden>
        <p>Kneading is a comforting behavior linked to kittenhood. Adult cats often do it when they feel safe, content, or especially cozy in a favorite spot.</p>
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="example">
      <button class="question" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="answer-5">
        <span class="question-text">What toys do cats usually enjoy?</span>
        <span class="icon" aria-hidden="true">+</span>
      </button>
      <div class="details" id="answer-5" hidden>
        <p>Interactive toys like feather wands, rolling balls, and puzzle feeders are popular because they mimic hunting behavior. Rotating toys keeps playtime fresh.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </main>

  <script>
    document.querySelectorAll('.example').forEach((example) => {
      const button = example.querySelector('.question');
      const details = example.querySelector('.details');

      button.addEventListener('click', () => {
        const expanded = button.getAttribute('aria-expanded') === 'true';
        button.setAttribute('aria-expanded', String(!expanded));
        details.hidden = expanded;
        example.classList.toggle('open', !expanded);
      });
    });
  </script>
</body>
</html>
